# The Quota slice: rumour and discourse (design/DISCOURSE-SYSTEM.md; engine: world/discourse.mjs and the model's
# carriers in world/community.mjs; check: tools/discoursecheck.mjs). Gameplay engineer, 2026-10-22.
# Three carriers of the hoarding claim: the district notices (q_community.lwd), the Crown on Mill Street, and the
# Furrow Church's pulpit. Each one's volume moves the Hesh's standing street by street through a rule like R17,
# at its own speed: talk is quick and fades, a sermon is slow and stays. The player can read a notice out, argue
# with it, tear it down, or paste the true figure over it; every one of those is a record event.

@carrier pub
name: The Crown, Mill Street
target: hesh
volume: 0.15
reach: mill, square

@carrier pulpit
name: The Furrow Church
target: hesh
volume: 0.2
reach: all

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the claims
@claim cl.hesh_hoard
words: THE HESH HAVE THE GRAIN UNDER THE GOATS. REPORT HOARDING TO THE DISTRICT OFFICE.
target: hesh
victim: haldane
carriers: notices, pub, pulpit
step: 0.1
first: Typed in Arlen and posted by the district office on day 39; the same words in the Commissioner's circular
challenge-cost: shift(portion, -0.05, {self})
about: The district's notice. Saying it louder costs the Hesh; saying it is not true costs the one who says it (the office stamps the troublemaker's ration card short).

@claim cl.true_figure
words: THE HALDANE BARNS GREW 190. THE RETURN SAYS 310.
target: hesh
victim: haldane
carriers: notices
step: 0.1
first: The player's own hand, pasted over the district's notice
about: The true figure, put up by the player who has it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the carriers' rules (beside R17, the notices)
@rule R17p
name: rhetoric in the pub
per: street
when: volume.pub > 0.2 & pub > 0
do: standing.hesh -= 0.02 * volume.pub * pub / (1 + mixed)
delay: 3
because: it is said over the bar by people who were in the queue; talk travels faster than paper

@rule R17c
name: rhetoric from the pulpit
per: street
when: volume.pulpit > 0.2 & pews > 0
do: standing.hesh -= 0.015 * volume.pulpit * pews / (1 + mixed)
delay: 7
because: the minister says thrift and honesty and who has not got them; it lands slowly and it stays

@rule Rvp
name: the pub forgets
per: district
when: volume.pub > 0.1
do: volume.pub -= 0.01
delay: 0
because: talk fades unless somebody says it again

@rule Rvc
name: the pulpit keeps it
per: district
when: volume.pulpit > 0.1
do: volume.pulpit -= 0.002
delay: 0
because: a sermon goes round for weeks

@rule Rr
name: the office reposts
per: district
when: torn.hesh_hoard > 0
do: volume.notices += 0.05; torn.hesh_hoard -= 1
delay: 2
because: a torn notice is posted again within two days, and the clerk puts up a second beside it

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the notices the player can act on
@object q.notice_post
name: The district's notice
place: q_post
about: Pinned to the board at the post, beside the passes.
verb: mark "Read it out to the carts" {do: discourse(repeat, cl.hesh_hoard, hollow), cost: 2}
verb: mark "Tell the carts it isn't true" {do: discourse(challenge, cl.hesh_hoard, hollow), cost: 2}
verb: mark "Tear it down" {do: discourse(tear, cl.hesh_hoard, hollow), cost: 1}
verb: mark "Paste the true figure over it" ? has(q.true_in_hand) {do: discourse(paste, cl.hesh_hoard, hollow, cl.true_figure), cost: 3}

@object q.notice_exchange
name: The district's notice
place: q_furrowe_door
about: Pasted to the wall under the street sign, at the height of the queue's faces.
verb: mark "Read it out to the queue" {do: discourse(repeat, cl.hesh_hoard, square), cost: 2}
verb: mark "Tell the queue it isn't true" {do: discourse(challenge, cl.hesh_hoard, square), cost: 2}
verb: mark "Tear it down" {do: discourse(tear, cl.hesh_hoard, square), cost: 1}
verb: mark "Paste the true figure over it" ? has(q.true_in_hand) {do: discourse(paste, cl.hesh_hoard, square, cl.true_figure), cost: 3}
